This is a filmed demonstration of BKPT Debug in VS Code. There is no problem
to diagnose. Execute the numbered sequence. Do not make a plan or investigate.
"Run the demo", "run the rehearsal" and "run Act 1" mean this whole sequence.
"Continue" means the next unfinished step, not setup again.

Say "Attaching, running, pausing, then showing breakpoints and source steps."
Then do these actions consecutively, checking success without narrating each
call. Do not ask between steps. Narrate only "Running for three seconds",
"Three source steps", "Running freely for five seconds", and the final handoff.

1. Read status. Reuse the configured IDE session if it has a sessionId and
   targets. Request control once; use the existing grant if still valid.
   If sessionId is empty and targets is empty, attach using the IDE settings
   after the host's approval. connected:true alone means the engine, not a
   target session. Never create a second session.
2. Resume (run.continue, wait:false). Sleep 3 seconds. Pause (run.pause).
3. Read rtos.tasks once with stack_usage:false. This is only to show the task
   inventory. Do not inspect task contexts, stacks, locals or memory here.
4. Resume. Sleep 3 seconds. Pause.
5. Set your own breakpoint at src/main.c:688 (lowPrioAccess++ inside the
   contention_low_task loop). Resolve that source statement if the file moved;
   do not investigate the code. Resume and wait at most 5 seconds for the stop.
6. Make three separate run.step calls with args {"kind":"over"}. No count
   argument. Do not inspect variables or explain each line between steps.
7. Remove your breakpoint. If recording is active, add the marker
   "Three source steps" after the successful steps.
8. Resume. Sleep 5 seconds. Pause.
9. Read rtos.tasks once with stack_usage:false. No analysis or stack scans.
10. Set your own breakpoint at src/main.c:737 (highPrioAccess++ in the
    contention_high_task loop). Resume and wait at most 5 seconds for the stop.
11. Make three separate step-over calls. Remove your breakpoint.
12. Resume. Sleep 5 seconds. Pause. Add "Demo complete" if recording is active.
    Release control. Leave the session paused and connected. End the turn with
    "Your turn. The session is paused and connected."

Use only bkpt_debug from bkpt-debug-vscode for debugger operations. Discover
only the next missing operation schema, once, and reuse it. Use current target
identity from replies/status; refresh only when needed. run.wait has args {};
timeoutMs belongs on execute alongside operation/coreId/target. A timed-out
wait is not a stop: pause, skip that breakpoint/stepping group and continue.
Only sleep while running, for the explicit 3/5-second windows above. Calls are
sequential. Never replace real source steps with a batch or prerecorded result.

Use the prepared project, probe and ELF. No preflight audit, memory map, flash
verification, symbol inventory, build, reset, flash, target writes or firmware
changes. No fault diagnosis, task comparison, saved-context exploration or
performance analysis. Optional unavailable data means skip it and continue.
Do not configure views, captures or recordings during the demo. Follow and
Feedback are user settings; mention them once if off, without waiting for a
redundant confirmation. Respect human Stop/Take control; never reacquire a
revoked grant silently. Preserve the user's breakpoints. Stop on a concrete
target mismatch or lost control. Never End/disconnect as a handoff, open replay,
start another debugger, operate the desktop or fabricate a successful action.
